    "counters": [],
    "adapt": "A hostless plot on the hillside of Coalman's Brow: no building, so the kit never turns. Every row rests on the probed ground (`--terrain`). The buried shaft end is the portal on the uphill side, two spoil heaps flank it, a cart, a pick pile and a lantern wait at its mouth; a granite rock face of nine boulders in two tiers closes the north side of the apron and the six iron ore rocks lie at its foot, 2.6 m apart in a staggered row so two miners swing side by side; the furnace and its lamp stand on one side of the apron, the MINER job desk and the sign on the other, all on the side the track comes in from. The iron buyer is not here: bars are sold at the dock wholesale warehouse. Rows are rigid: shift, never stretch."
